Here’s a quick Java snippet that shows how you’d prepare the `CallableStatement` on your `ProxyConnection` instance (`proxyConn`) with the exact flags you requested:

```java
import java.sql.*;

public class TotalSalesExample {

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        // Assume proxyConn is already instantiated and connected
        ProxyConnection proxyConn = /* obtain your proxy connection here */;

        // Prepare the CALL statement with the desired result‑set characteristics
        CallableStatement cs = proxyConn.prepareCall(
                "CALL totalSales(?)",
                ResultSet.TYPE_SCROLL_INSENSITIVE,   // scrollable but not sensitive to changes
                ResultSet.CONCUR_READ_ONLY,          // read‑only cursor
                ResultSet.CLOSE_CURSORS_AT_COMMIT);  // close cursors when transaction commits

        // Bind the input parameter (if needed)
        cs.setInt(1, 12345);   // example: pass an ID or whatever your proc expects

        // Execute the stored procedure
        boolean hasResults = cs.execute();

        // Process the result set(s) if any
        while (hasResults) {
            try (ResultSet rs = cs.getResultSet()) {
                while (rs.next()) {
                    // Example: retrieve columns from the result set
                    int id = rs.getInt("id");
                    double amount = rs.getDouble("amount");
                    System.out.printf("ID: %d, Amount: %.2f%n", id, amount);
                }
            }
            hasResults = cs.getMoreResults();
        }

        // Clean up
        cs.close();
    }
}
```

### What this does

| Parameter | Meaning |
|-----------|---------|
| `"CALL totalSales(?)"` | The SQL string that calls your stored procedure. Replace the placeholder `?` with the actual number of parameters your procedure requires. |
| `ResultSet.TYPE_SCROLL_INSENSITIVE` | Allows the cursor to move forwards/backwards without reflecting changes made after the cursor was positioned. |
| `ResultSet.CONCUR_READ_ONLY` | The cursor cannot be used to update rows. |
| `ResultSet.CLOSE_CURSORS_AT_COMMIT` | Cursors will automatically close when the transaction commits. |

